-- title:
--   Total degree equals index of the conjugated level
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with finite residue field and fraction field $K_0$, and let $\mathcal T =$ `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀` be the graph on homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2$ with adjacency generated by `AdjacentLattice`, on which $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ acts by graph automorphisms. Fix $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ and two subgroups $\Gamma_d,\Gamma_c \le G$ whose images $H_d = \rho(\Gamma_d)$, $H_c = \rho(\Gamma_c)$ preserve the type `vertexType` (graph distance from `stdVertex` mod $2$) and have finite stabilisers of every dart. Let $D_d$ on finite $(E_d,V_d)$ and $D_c$ on finite $(E_c,V_c)$ be degeneracy data (maps $a,b$ to vertices and widths $w \in \mathbb N^+$), presented through equivalences $e_{V}$ of the vertex-orbit quotients with $V_d$, $V_c$ and $e_{E}$ of the sets of dart-orbits whose chosen representative has first vertex of type $0$ with $E_d$, $E_c$, such that $a$, $b$ compute the orbits of the origin and terminus of the representative dart and $w$ its stabiliser order. Let $g \in G$ have type-preserving image $p = \rho(g)$ and satisfy $\Gamma_d \le g\Gamma_c g^{-1}$, and let $\mu : D_d \to D_c$ be a `FiniteHom`, i.e. level maps compatible with $a$ and $b$, local degrees $\deg$ with $w(\mu e) = \deg(e)\, w(e)$, vertex degrees whose fibre sums over each degeneracy map are constant, and a total degree whose fibre sums recover it; assume that through the presentations $\mu$ is induced on vertex- and dart-orbits by $x \mapsto p^{-1}\cdot x$. Then the total degree of $\mu$ equals the index in $H_c$ of the subgroup $\{x \in H_c : p\,x\,p^{-1} \in H_d\}$.
--
--   This identifies the degree of a harmonic morphism between the two folded quotient graphs $H_d\backslash\mathcal T$ and $H_c\backslash\mathcal T$, arising from an arrow given by conjugation by $g$, with the index of the conjugated level $p^{-1}H_d p \cap H_c$ in $H_c$; it is the degree bookkeeping needed for the degeneracy maps between Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformised curves. It is used in the computation of pushforwards and pullbacks of degree-zero divisor classes on Mumford quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_Mumford_finiteHom_degTotal_eq_index_of_mumfordQuotient_conj.lean

